## Ecosystem Overview

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Proprietary & Private API Notice**
> The Lament ecosystem and its underlying API services are **private and non-open-source**. Public third-party API access is strictly disabled to protect system integrity, preserve server resource allocations, and operate within tight Edge infrastructure quotas.

Lament is a high-performance music streaming ecosystem engineered for zero-latency audio playback, automated metadata extraction, and strict access security. 

Rather than a monolithic codebase, Lament is decoupled into specialized repositories under the **lamentfm** organization:

| Repository | Role | Tech Stack | Key Functionality |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `lament` | Web Frontend Client | SvelteKit, Svelte 5, Tailwind CSS v4, HLS.js | SSR, reactive player, glassmorphism UI, server-side API proxying |
| `lament-api` | Edge REST Backend | Hono, Cloudflare Workers, Turso LibSQL, R2 | Dual-layer auth, ETag caching, HLS manifests, maintenance flags |
| `lament-scrapper` | Ingestion Pipeline | Node.js, Bun, `yt-dlp`, `sharp`, Spotify, Last.fm, Deezer, iTunes | Audio extraction without re-encoding, image optimization, LRC parsing |
| `lament-docs` | Documentation App | SvelteKit, Svelte 5, MDsveX | Complete developer reference, architecture specs, and API contracts |
| `lament-mobile` | Mobile Client | Flutter, Dart | Native iOS and Android player with offline cache support |
| `lament-admin` | Management Portal | SvelteKit, Tailwind CSS | Content management, client key administration, and analytics |
| `calibrate` | Lyric Alignment Tool | Python, `stable-whisper`, FFmpeg | Forced-alignment AI model for re-syncing misaligned LRC lyrics |

---

## Architectural Principles

### 1. Zero Direct Backend Exposure (Proxy Architecture)
The browser and client apps never communicate directly with the core database or administrative endpoints. All web requests are routed through SvelteKit server-side proxy routes (`+server.ts`), which inject client authentication credentials (`x-api-key`) and sanitize response headers.

### 2. Native Quality Lossless Extraction
The scraper pipeline extracts raw audio streams (`.m4a` AAC / Opus `.webm`) directly from YouTube sources via `yt-dlp`. Audio is wrapped in native containers without lossy re-encoding to prevent transcoding generational loss.

### 3. Edge-First HLS Delivery
Audio files are split into HLS segments (`.ts`) and manifests (`.m3u8`) hosted on Cloudflare R2 object storage (`cdn.lament.rynds.my.id`). Direct unauthorized hotlinking is blocked at the Cloudflare edge via WAF Referer validation rules.

### 4. Distributed State & Caching
Metadata resides in Turso LibSQL (SQLite at the edge), while high-frequency read requests leverage LRU in-memory caches and HTTP ETag validation (`304 Not Modified`).
